# SPDX-License-Identifier: MPL-2.0
# One plan drawing for the live plan and a sheet's plan viewport (drawing
# quality plan, item 6): both record the same sequence through these
# functions, the live plan for the active storey, a sheet's viewport for its
# view's own storey. `planEditor` is an editor whose storey (`levelId`),
# plan view (`planViewId`), rules (`planRules`) and rooms (`spaces`) are
# those of the plan drawn; the sheet makes one from the editor for its view.
import ui/panels/bim_plan_panel.dl
import ui/panels/bim_plan_projection.dl

# Keeps the imported elements of `importShown` on `editor` for its plans:
# their meshes and the elevation of the storey each is contained in, so that
# a plan of any storey draws those of its storey (`append bim linked element
# lines of`) without the import itself.
function keep bim linked elements of {bim import record:importShown} in {a pointer to a bim editor record:editor}:
    execute:
        set elevations to a cad topology list of a 64 bit floating-point number
        loop cursor from 0 to the length of (importShown's meshes's values):
            set entry to the item at cursor in (importShown's meshes's values)
            append (the bim storey elevation of mesh entry in editor's documentValue's current with importShown) to (elevations's values)
        set editor's importedMeshes to importShown's meshes
        set editor's importedStoreys to elevations

# Appends the plan lines (`append bim plan lines of`) of the imported
# elements kept on `planEditor` (`keep bim linked elements of`) that stand on its
# storey and that its plan rules show, cut at its plan's cut height: the cut
# to `cutLines`, the edges below it to `belowLines`.
function append bim linked element lines of {bim editor record:planEditor} into {a pointer to a list:cutLines} and {a pointer to a list:belowLines}:
    execute:
        set storeyHeight to the bim storey elevation of planEditor
        set storeyMeshes to a cad topology list of a bim scene mesh record
        set kept to the minimum of (the length of (planEditor's importedMeshes's values)) and (the length of (planEditor's importedStoreys's values))
        loop cursor from 0 to kept:
            # A mesh in no storey has no elevation (not a number) and is
            # left out, as `the bim meshes of … on storey at` leaves it out.
            if (the absolute value of ((the item at cursor in (planEditor's importedStoreys's values)) - storeyHeight)) < 0.001:
                append (the item at cursor in (planEditor's importedMeshes's values)) to (storeyMeshes's values)
        if (the length of (storeyMeshes's values)) = 0:
            return nothing
        set noMeshes to a cad topology list of a bim scene mesh record
        set planMeshes to the bim meshes of (noMeshes's values) and (storeyMeshes's values) shown by planEditor's planRules
        append bim plan lines of (planMeshes's values) cut at (storeyHeight + (the bim plan cut height of planEditor)) into cutLines and belowLines

# What a plan shows under its symbols, recorded on `canvas` through
# `transform`, in the view's sketchy lines when it asks for them:
#
# - the room fills, where the plan shows spaces (the model review only);
# - on screen the walls of the storey below, an underlay to draw over, which
#   a sheet leaves out;
# - the hatched cut `cutView` (the evaluation cut at the plan's height);
# - openings, sketches (on paper with the view's referenced vectors, which
#   the screen draws retained), linear elements (on paper only the tagged
#   reinforcement), stairs (`stairCache`; the screen keeps one construction
#   detail at every zoom), opening details;
# - the folded components among `sceneMeshes`, and the imported elements'
#   plan lines `linkedCut` and `linkedBelow` (`append bim linked element
#   lines of`);
# - under the cut, what the plan sees beyond it (`bim_plan_projection.dl`):
#   the edges below it thin, those above it dashed, kept in
#   `planProjection` until what they show changes.
#
# The slab and roof edges are not recorded here: the screen draws them every
# frame so that they follow a dragged slab (`draw bim slabs`), a sheet
# records them first (`record bim slab edges`).
function record bim plan of {bim editor record:planEditor} cut as {bim view record:cutView} among {a pointer to a list:sceneMeshes} with linked {a pointer to a list:linkedCut} and {a pointer to a list:linkedBelow} keeping {a pointer to a bim curtain plan cache record:stairCache} projecting {a pointer to a bim plan projection record:planProjection} through {bim drawing transform record:transform} using {bim text atlas record:typeface} on {a pointer to a bim canvas record:canvas}:
    execute:
        set modelValue to planEditor's documentValue's current
        set onPaper to canvas's paperScale > 0.0
        set wasSketchy to canvas's sketchy
        set canvas's sketchy to bim view planEditor's planViewId is sketchy in modelValue
        if bim category bim space category is visible in planEditor's planRules:
            draw bim space fills of planEditor through transform on canvas
        if (onPaper = false) and (bim category bim wall category is visible in planEditor's planRules):
            draw bim storey below of planEditor through transform on canvas
        refresh bim plan projection in planProjection of planEditor among sceneMeshes cut as cutView
        record bim plan projection planProjection of planEditor through transform on canvas
        draw bim hatched cut faces of cutView for planEditor through transform as section false following planEditor's planRules on canvas
        draw bim openings in plan of planEditor through transform on canvas
        draw bim sketches of planEditor through transform on canvas using typeface referencing onPaper
        draw bim linears in plan of planEditor through transform with all reinforcement (onPaper = false) on canvas
        set detailScale to 250.0
        if onPaper:
            set detailScale to transform's scale
        draw bim stairs in plan of planEditor through transform on canvas keeping stairCache at detail scale detailScale
        draw bim opening details of planEditor through transform on canvas
        draw bim folded components in plan of planEditor among sceneMeshes through transform on canvas
        record bim plan lines linkedCut and linkedBelow through transform on canvas
        set canvas's sketchy to wasSketchy

# The same, its projection worked out afresh (a sheet's viewport, which is
# recorded again only when the model changes).
function record bim plan of {bim editor record:planEditor} cut as {bim view record:cutView} among {a pointer to a list:sceneMeshes} with linked {a pointer to a list:linkedCut} and {a pointer to a list:linkedBelow} keeping {a pointer to a bim curtain plan cache record:stairCache} through {bim drawing transform record:transform} using {bim text atlas record:typeface} on {a pointer to a bim canvas record:canvas}:
    execute:
        set freshProjection to an empty bim plan projection
        record bim plan of planEditor cut as cutView among sceneMeshes with linked linkedCut and linkedBelow keeping stairCache projecting (the address of freshProjection) through transform using typeface on canvas

# What a plan shows over it, recorded on `canvas` through `transform`: the
# room labels (where the plan shows spaces) at the places `labelPlaces`
# (`append bim room label places of`), grids, section marks, the
# annotations its drawing type applies (pile numbers and table, beam
# labels, pile tip levels), the NEN 2580 area measures where its drawing
# type asks for them, level marks, dimensions and tags, lettered
# `textHeight` canvas units high. Dimensions come after the labels and
# marks, so that their values keep clear of them.
function record bim plan symbols of {bim editor record:planEditor} placing labels at {a pointer to a list:labelPlaces} through {bim drawing transform record:transform} lettered at {a 64 bit floating-point number:textHeight} on {a pointer to a bim canvas record:canvas}:
    execute:
        if bim category bim space category is visible in planEditor's planRules:
            draw bim space labels of planEditor placed at labelPlaces through transform lettered at textHeight on canvas
        draw bim grids in plan of planEditor through transform on canvas
        draw bim section marks in plan of planEditor through transform on canvas
        draw bim annotations in plan of planEditor through transform on canvas
        draw bim area measures in plan of planEditor through transform on canvas
        draw bim level marks in plan of planEditor placed at labelPlaces through transform lettered at textHeight on canvas
        draw bim dimensions in plan of planEditor through transform on canvas
        draw bim tags in plan of planEditor through transform on canvas

# The same with the label places found for the plan now (a sheet's plan;
# the window keeps them, found again only when the plan changes).
function record bim plan symbols of {bim editor record:planEditor} through {bim drawing transform record:transform} lettered at {a 64 bit floating-point number:textHeight} on {a pointer to a bim canvas record:canvas}:
    execute:
        set foundPlaces to an empty list of a cad vector2
        append bim room label places of planEditor into foundPlaces
        record bim plan symbols of planEditor placing labels at foundPlaces through transform lettered at textHeight on canvas
        free foundPlaces
